    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6d28f7b3-b12a-5cc5-b3b7-558542d479f1",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $det(F)=0$\n- **III.** $det(F)=-4$\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\sqrt{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}- \\sqrt{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\sqrt{2})|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}- \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 4 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{2}|\\begin{aligned}- \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\sqrt{2})(- 2 \\sqrt{2}+0)+0+\\frac{1}{2}(0-8) \\\\  & =(- \\sqrt{2})\\cdot (- 2 \\sqrt{2})+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true.",
