    "question": {
      ":question/id": "88b807aa-9017-5cfe-8d7e-02d5b1dc5499",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(F)=\\frac{26}{35}$\n- **II.** $det(F)=-3$\n- **III.** $F$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{3}{5} & - \\frac{3}{5} & - \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ \\frac{4}{7} & \\frac{2}{7} & - \\frac{3}{7}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{3}{5} & - \\frac{3}{5} & - \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ \\frac{4}{7} & \\frac{2}{7} & - \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3}{5})|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & - \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{3}{5}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ \\frac{4}{7} & - \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{2}{5})|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ \\frac{4}{7} & \\frac{2}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3}{5})(- \\frac{6}{7}+\\frac{6}{7})+\\frac{3}{5}(- \\frac{6}{7}+\\frac{12}{7})+(- \\frac{2}{5})(\\frac{4}{7}- \\frac{8}{7}) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3}{5})\\cdot 0+\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{6}{7}+(- \\frac{2}{5})\\cdot (- \\frac{4}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{35}+\\frac{8}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=\\frac{26}{35}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1ed6a19c-c0c7-5da5-96dd-16b6ab54c95b",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
