    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a6619fc8-89d8-5e2e-8524-950c5fe16e41",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $P$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $det(P)=1$\n- **III.** $det(P)=0$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - 2 \\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - 2 \\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}- 2 \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 4 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{1}{2})|\\begin{aligned}- 2 \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(- \\sqrt{2}+0)+0+(- \\frac{1}{2})(0-4) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (- \\sqrt{2})+(- \\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-2+2 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f98504e2-4efc-5175-bbec-950c4693564f",
